        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Michigan gubernatorial election, 2006\n- People: Jennifer Granholm, Dick DeVos, Ruth Johnson, Porter Hazelton\n- Roles: Governor of Michigan, lieutenant governor candidate, Michigan House of Representatives member, businessman, politician, author\n\nFacts:\n- The Michigan gubernatorial election of 2006 was one of 36 U.S. gubernatorial elections held on November 7, 2006.\n- Porter Hazelton was born on November 15, 1812, and he was a Michigan politician.\n- Porter Hazelton died on August 15, 1870.\n- Dick DeVos was born on October 21, 1955, and he is an American entrepreneur-businessman and author from Michigan.\n- In 2006, incumbent Democratic Governor Jennifer Granholm was re-elected over Republican businessman Dick DeVos and three minor party candidates.\n- In 2006, Ruth Johnson was the Republican candidate for lieutenant governor as Dick DeVos's running mate.\n- Ruth Johnson is a former member of the Michigan House of Representatives.",
